WEBVTT

1
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Daniel K.: Did the funnel breakdown come through?

2
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Emma C.: It did. I put it on the ticket last night.

3
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Emma C.: Step data is in. 28% of signups stop at "connect your calendar", the largest single drop.

4
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
Daniel K.: And email two talks about reminders, which only matter after the first booking.

5
00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Emma C.: So email two is the wrong email at the wrong time.

6
00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.000
Daniel K.: What should email two say instead?

7
00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.000
Emma C.: Connect your calendar, and how long it takes.

8
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:29.000
Emma C.: The calendar instructions move into email two, with a 60-second video. I'll rewrite email two this week, calendar first.

9
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.000
Daniel K.: Keep the video under a minute.

10
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.000
Emma C.: Sixty seconds, promise.

11
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.000
Daniel K.: Where do reminders go, then?

12
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:49.000
Emma C.: Later. Nobody needs a reminder before their first booking.

13
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:12.000
Emma C.: So email two becomes the calendar-connect email, and reminders move to email four.

14
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Daniel K.: Email four works.

15
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:28.000
Emma C.: Then email two has one job.

16
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:25.000
Emma C.: Will a better email fix the drop on its own?

17
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Daniel K.: I doubt it.

18
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.000
Daniel K.: The biggest drop is a setup step, not a pricing step. Copy alone won't fix it.

19
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:16.000
Emma C.: So we need something in the app as well.

20
00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:25.000
Daniel K.: Right where people get stuck.

21
00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:09.000
Emma C.: What would the in-app part look like?

22
00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:29.000
Daniel K.: Something small on the dashboard, right after signup.

23
00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:54.000
Daniel K.: An in-app checklist makes the same point without waiting for the email, so let me sketch a checklist, three items, nothing more.

24
00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.000
Emma C.: Three is plenty.

25
00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.000
Daniel K.: I'll start from the calendar step.

26
00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:09.000
Emma C.: One thing: let's keep the names consistent.

27
00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.000
Daniel K.: Good point.

28
00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.000
Emma C.: Then the emails and the checklist use the same three step names.

29
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.000
Daniel K.: Same names, agreed.

30
00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:53.000
Emma C.: Mine are: connect your calendar, set your hours, take a booking.

31
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:39.000
Daniel K.: Email three still links the old video.

32
00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:52.000
Emma C.: Give me a second.

33
00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Emma C.: Done: I've just removed the outdated video link from email three.

34
00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.000
Daniel K.: Thanks.

35
00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.000
Emma C.: That's all from me.
